STUDIO WEBSITE - Implementation Summary
=====================================

Pages created:
- index.html (Home page with all sections)

Sections included:
1. Home/Hero section - with main CTA leading to Contact
2. Work section - with project grid (2 placeholder projects)
3. About section - with team info and stats
4. Contact section - with form and contact info

Navigation:
- Top nav links: Work, About, Contact (all reachable)
- Hero CTA: "Get in touch" links to #contact
- Footer nav: Work, About, Contact

Accessibility features:
- Skip link for keyboard navigation
- ARIA labels on form elements, navigation, main content
- Focus-visible styles
- Form validation with accessible error feedback
- Semantic HTML structure
- Label association with form inputs

Responsive design:
- Mobile: 390px - hamburger menu, stacked layout
- Tablet: 768px - 2-column about section, full grid
- Desktop: 1440px - full layout, max-width containment

Placeholder copy documented:
- [city] in About section needs client input
- hello@studio.example email placeholder
- Location [City, State] placeholder
- Project descriptions are honest placeholders

Forms:
- Visible labels for all inputs
- Accessible validation feedback (border color changes, error states)
- Required attributes on all form fields
- No actual submission service - placeholder only

Files created:
- studio-site/index.html
- studio-site/style.css  
- studio-site/script.js

Remaining issues:
- None - implementation is complete

Run instructions:
1. Open studio-site/index.html in a browser
2. Or serve locally: npx serve studio-site
3. Navigation works via anchor links (#work, #about, #contact)
